From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a site can offer a passkey an extension holds

Google asked to create a passkey the user's Bitwarden already held, and
Bitwarden's passkey in its autofill menu did nothing when clicked. Patch
0048 answered isConditionalMediationAvailable() false, so a site never
started the conditional get() a passkey extension's autofill answers;
and a site that started one anyway was refused at once, because the
browser has no WebAuthn delegate. Bitwarden races its own answer against
the browser's, so the refusal won and the page had stopped listening by
the time the user picked a passkey.

- The override answers what content does: no platform authenticator on
  Linux, and conditional UI wherever no extension proxies the origin.
- A conditional request with no delegate is held until the site aborts
  it, as Chrome holds one its autofill has nothing for. A modal request
  is still refused.
---
 .../chrome_web_authentication_delegate.cc      | 18 +++++++-----------
 .../webauth/authenticator_common_impl.cc       |  8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 15 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/webauthn/chrome_web_authentication_delegate.cc b/chrome/browser/webauthn/chrome_web_authentication_delegate.cc
index 8d3bfe9875..456b46e4f9 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/webauthn/chrome_web_authentication_delegate.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/webauthn/chrome_web_authentication_delegate.cc
@@ -257,19 +257,15 @@ void ChromeWebAuthenticationDelegate::
     IsUserVerifyingPlatformAuthenticatorAvailableOverride(
         content::RenderFrameHost* render_frame_host,
         base::OnceCallback<void(std::optional<bool>)> callback) {
-  // Domicile's engine fork: no platform authenticator and no conditional UI,
-  // because the browser draws neither. A site that asks is told no, so it
-  // offers what a passkey extension lends it rather than a sign-in the
-  // browser would refuse. The testing API's answer still wins, as upstream.
+  // Domicile's engine fork: content's own answers, which upstream's override
+  // here only ever adds the browser's passkeys to -- and the browser offers
+  // none. On Linux that is no platform authenticator, and conditional UI
+  // wherever no extension proxies the origin: a passkey extension draws the
+  // autofill a site's conditional get() waits on, and content holds that
+  // request until the site aborts it. The testing API's answer still wins.
   content::WebAuthenticationDelegate::
       IsUserVerifyingPlatformAuthenticatorAvailableOverride(
-          render_frame_host,
-          base::BindOnce(
-              [](base::OnceCallback<void(std::optional<bool>)> callback,
-                 std::optional<bool> testing_api_override) {
-                std::move(callback).Run(testing_api_override.value_or(false));
-              },
-              std::move(callback)));
+          render_frame_host, std::move(callback));
 }
 
 content::WebAuthenticationRequestProxy*
diff --git a/content/browser/webauth/authenticator_common_impl.cc b/content/browser/webauth/authenticator_common_impl.cc
index bd7a62ddcf..56fc837f4d 100644
--- a/content/browser/webauth/authenticator_common_impl.cc
+++ b/content/browser/webauth/authenticator_common_impl.cc
@@ -1892,6 +1892,14 @@ void AuthenticatorCommonImpl::ContinueGetAssertionAfterRpIdCheck(
 
   req_state_->request_delegate = MaybeCreateRequestDelegate();
   if (!req_state_->request_delegate) {
+    // Domicile's engine fork: the browser draws no WebAuthn UI, so it has no
+    // delegate, and a conditional request is held rather than refused -- as
+    // Chrome holds one nothing in its autofill answers -- until the site
+    // aborts it. A passkey extension wrapping navigator.credentials races
+    // its own answer against this one, and a refusal won the race.
+    if (req_state_->mode == AuthenticationRequestMode::kConditional) {
+      return;
+    }
     req_state_->request_outcome = GetAssertionOutcome::kOtherFailure;
     CompleteGetAssertionRequest(
         blink::mojom::AuthenticatorStatus::PENDING_REQUEST);
